    },
    {
      "id": "54ff655a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Installing and loading packages\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "28c904d3",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Introduction\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3a2bc3cf",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Julia packages** are an organized collections of ready-made functions, classes and objects for providing solutions to various tasks. **Julia** packages are distributed as modules, which can be installed using the `Pkg` package manager and used in your projects.\n\nIn **AnyMath**, working with **Julia** packages is also carried out via the built-in `Pkg` package manager.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7b90f1bf",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### How to work with packages\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f4e4f54c",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Find the exact name of the package you are interested in. The **Julia** ecosystem contains over $10,000$ packages registered in the central registry, which can make finding the right package quite difficult. To optimise your search, we recommend consulting the following sources:\n\n* [Practical Applications](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/en/external-libs.html) is a section of the **AnyMath** documentation, which describes a large number of packages.\n* [JuliaHub](https://juliahub.com/ui/Packages) is a service for searching across all registered documentation for open-source packages, with the option to sort by tags and keywords.\n* [Julia Packages](https://juliapackages.com/) is an online resource designed for searching, exploring and viewing **Julia** packages, with the option to apply filters by category, popularity and date.\n* [Julia.jl](https://github.com/svaksha/Julia.jl) is the main package repository for the **Julia**. This repository is hosted on the **GitHub** platform and contains a wealth of useful packages and tools developed by the community for working with the **Julia**.\n\nGet started with packages in **Julia** by adding the `Pkg` package manager.\n\nAdd packages to your environment using the `add` command so that you can use them in your project.\n\nLoad a package into a namespace and access its specific elements using the `using` and `import` commands. You can also add your own packages.\n\nIf necessary, check the status of packages using `status` and remove any unwanted ones using the `remove` or `rm` commands.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "09975105",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Working with **Julia** packages in the script editor\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dd2505d6",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "To install a new package in an **AnyMath** interactive script, run the command `Pkg.add(\"Package name\")`. For example, the section of code to add the `Example` package would look like this:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "49383a73",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Pkg.add(\"Example\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "943b6bc5",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Once this cell is run, the `Example` package will be installed. Information on the progress of the package installation will be displayed automatically:\n\n```julia\nResolving package versions...\nInstalled Example ─ v0.5.3\nUpdating `/user/start/Project.toml`\n[7876af07] + Example v0.5.3\nUpdating `/user/start/Manifest.toml`\n[7876af07] + Example v0.5.3\n```\n\nYou can add several packages at once by listing their names separated by commas and enclosing them in square brackets to form an array of strings, for example:\n\n```\nPkg.add([\"Example\", \"Plots\"])\n```\n\nTo remove a package, use the `rm` command:\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dde97a1c",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "Pkg.rm(\"Example\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 0,
      "outputs": [],
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false,
          "outputInfo": {
            "isExpanded": false,
            "scrollTop": 0
          },
          "maskInfo": {
            "isMaskVisible": true,
            "isEditorVisible": true,
            "isAutoplayActive": false
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c22d038e",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "To remove several packages at once, list their names separated by commas and enclosed in square brackets:\n\n```julia\nPkg.rm([\"Example\", \"Plots\"])\n```\n\nThe `remove` command is not defined in the script editor, although it is used in the command line. Attempting to call the `remove` command in the script editor will result in an error.\n\n{% note info \"Note\" %}\n\n**Julia** package names are case-sensitive and must begin with a capital letter; otherwise, you will receive an error message.\n\n{% endnote %}\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
