        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6614da27",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "* [`Plots.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/juliaplots/index.html) is the main package designed for data visualization (for plotting various types of graphs based on numerical data).\n* [`PlotlyJS.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/PlotlyJS/index.html) is a package for data visualization. It provides additional capabilities for creating interactive graphs and saving graphs to files.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1a1cf517",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### System packages\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f4429028",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "* [`Matlab.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/MATLAB/readme.html) – allows you to call **MATLAB** functions from **Julia**.\r\n* [`PyCall.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/PyCall/readme.html) – allows you to call **Python** from **Julia**.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c0478084",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Working with file formats\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c197b9e9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "* [`MAT.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/MAT/index.html) is a package providing tools for reading and writing data files in the **MATLAB** format to **Julia**.\n* [`JLD2.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/JLD2.html) – this package allows you to save and load data structures **Julia** in a format that is a subset of the HDF5 standard.\n* [`XLSX.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/XLSX.html) is a package for reading and writing **Excel** spreadsheet files.\n* [`CSV.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/CSV.html) is a package for working with delimited text data, whether comma-separated (CSV), tab-separated (TSV) or separated by another character.\n* [`FileIO.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/FileIO.html) – this package provides a general framework for defining file formats and dispatching to the appropriate read and write methods. The two main functions in this package are called `load` and `save`. They provide high-level support for formatted files, in contrast to the low-level `read` and `write` functions in **Julia**.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cfa361fe",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Mathematical packages\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": true,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ee7fb810",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "* [`LinearAlgebra.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/stdlib/LinearAlgebra.html) – this package contains a wide range of functions for solving linear algebra problems.\n* [`Roots.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Roots.html) – this package contains functions for solving equations of the form $f(x)=0$. \n* [`DifferentialEquations.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/DifferentialEquations/index.html) is a package for the numerical solution of ordinary differential equations.\n* [`NumericalIntegration.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/NumericalIntegration/README.html) is a package for the numerical integration of discretized data.\n* [`ControlSystems.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/ControlSystems/index.html) is a package containing functions for the analysis and synthesis of control systems (primarily linear ones).\n* [`Interpolations.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Interpolations/index.html) is a package containing functions for various interpolation methods.\n* [`DynamicalSystems.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/DynamicalSystems/index.html) is a package containing functions for solving non-linear dynamics problems and analyzing time series.\n* [`Calculus.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Calculus/README.html) is a package containing functions for basic differentiation and integration operations.\n* [`GLPK.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/GLPK/README.html) is a package containing functions for linear programming and linear optimization.\n* [`Ipopt.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Ipopt/README.html) is a package for the non-linear optimization of high-dimensional problems.\n* [`Distributions.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Distributions/index.html) is a package containing functions for various probability distributions.\n* [`Polynomials.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Polynomials.html) – this package provides basic arithmetic operations, integration, differentiation, evaluation, root-finding and approximation for one-dimensional polynomials.\n* [`TaylorSeries.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/TaylorSeries/index.html) is a package containing functions for Taylor series expansions of functions of one or two variables.\n* [`NLSolve.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/NLsolve/README.html) is a package containing functions for solving systems of non-linear equations.\n* [`Symbolics.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Symbolics/manual.html) is a package for symbolic computation.\n* [`Flux.jl`](https://engee.com/helpcenter/stable/julia/Flux/index.html) is a package for machine learning.\n\n"
      ],
      "attachments": {},
      "metadata": {
        "name": "Section title",
        "engee": {
          "isDisplay": true,
          "isParagraph": false,
          "isClosedParagraph": false,
          "amountHideCellsInside": 0,
          "codeOutputView": "col",
          "codeOutputHidden": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
